hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20546","Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Barid, narrated to us, from Abu Bishr al-Halabi, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah, from his father, he said: Rain befell the people on a Friday, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered, and it was called out: Prayer today, or Friday today, is in the dwellings."
"20547","Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Nafi' ibn 'Umar ibn Jamil al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: I saw 'Ata' and Ibn Abi Mulaykah and 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid stoning the Jamrah before dawn on the day of sacrifice, so his father said to him: O Abu Sulayman, in which year did you hear from Nafi' ibn 'Umar? He said: In the year one hundred and sixty-nine, the year of al-Husayn's battle."
"20548","Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Nafi' ibn 'Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, concerning His saying, Blessed and Exalted is He: And do not bestow favor seeking more, he said: Do not give a thing seeking more than it."
"20549","Nuh ibn Habib narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath ibn Talq ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Tha'labah ibn 'Asim, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How wonderful is the believer; Allah does not decree anything for him except that it is good for him."
